<section id="about" class="section about">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h-section">Early, and careful, in equal measure.</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="about__prose">
      <p>
        I didn't arrive at this from theory. At the NBA I built the live scores tens of millions of
        people opened the app to check, and learned that systems beat heroics when something has to
        work every single night. I co-founded Bar Savvy and ran it as CTO, often its only engineer,
        which taught me to build leverage instead of just working longer. I've done that and my work
        at LV Collective in the same years, where I now spend as much time teaching the team to build
        with AI as I do building Sidekick OS to give them more to work with.
      </p>
      <p>
        I build this way for one reason: it lets a small team move like a much larger one, without
        the mess that usually comes with moving fast. It's why a deploy that used to eat the better
        part of an hour now takes about a minute, and why the people I hand this to start shipping
        work they couldn't before. The harness is what makes the speed safe enough to trust.
      </p>
      <p>
        Strip away the tooling and here's what's left: someone early to how software gets built now,
        and careful with it in equal measure. I like being at the front of this. I like even more
        that the things I build actually run. That's the work I want to keep doing, ideally next to
        people who want to be early and careful too.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

